---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import RoastMyPromptTool from '../components/RoastMyPromptTool';

import PricingSection from '../components/PricingSection';

Astro.response.headers.set('Cache-Control', 's-maxage=300, stale-while-revalidate=3600');
---
<Layout
  title="Roast My Prompt — Free AI Prompt Quality Checker"
  description="Paste any AI prompt and get an instant quality score with specific fixes for clarity, specificity, context, format, and constraints. Free, no sign-up."
>
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-14 pb-10 text-center border-b-2 border-[#1c1c1c]">
    <h1 class="text-5xl font-bold text-[#1a1a1a] leading-tight mb-5">Roast My Prompt</h1>
    <p class="text-[#6b6559] text-lg max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-8 leading-relaxed">
      Paste any ChatGPT, Claude, or AI prompt and get an instant quality score across five dimensions — with specific fixes and an improved version ready to copy. Free prompt checker, no sign-up.
    </p>
    <a href="#root" class="inline-block px-10 py-4 bg-[#f0b429] border-2 border-[#1c1c1c] rounded-xl font-bold text-[#1a1a1a] text-lg hover:brightness-95 transition-all">
      Roast My Prompt — Free
    </a>
    <p class="text-[#6b6559] text-sm mt-3">3 free generations per day — no credit card required</p>
  </section>

  <div id="root">
    <RoastMyPromptTool client:only="react" />
  </div>

  <div class="px-6 py-12 space-y-6">
    

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div class="border border-[#c8c0a8] rounded-xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#1a1a1a] mb-3">What gets scored</h2>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="mt-0.5">🎯</span><p class="text-[#6b6559] text-sm"><strong class="text-[#1a1a1a]">Clarity</strong> — does the task verb appear upfront, or is it buried in a soft opener?</p></div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="mt-0.5">🔍</span><p class="text-[#6b6559] text-sm"><strong class="text-[#1a1a1a]">Specificity</strong> — are requirements concrete, or does it rely on vague words the model has to interpret?</p></div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="mt-0.5">🧠</span><p class="text-[#6b6559] text-sm"><strong class="text-[#1a1a1a]">Context</strong> — is there a role frame, target audience, or background that helps the model calibrate?</p></div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="mt-0.5">📐</span><p class="text-[#6b6559] text-sm"><strong class="text-[#1a1a1a]">Format</strong> — does it specify how the output should be structured and how long?</p></div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="mt-0.5">🚧</span><p class="text-[#6b6559] text-sm"><strong class="text-[#1a1a1a]">Constraints</strong> — does it set tone, and specify what to avoid or exclude?</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-[#c8c0a8] rounded-xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#1a1a1a] mb-3">Why prompts fail</h2>
        <p class="text-[#6b6559] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Most AI prompts produce mediocre output not because the model is incapable, but because the prompt leaves too many decisions to the model. When you don't specify format, the model picks one. When you don't set context, the model assumes the most generic interpretation. When you don't add constraints, it hedges and adds filler.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[#6b6559] text-sm leading-relaxed mt-3">
          The five dimensions this tool scores are the same ones used by the <a href="/chatgpt-prompt-generator" class="text-[#1a1a1a] underline decoration-[#f0b429] underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#f0b429]">ChatGPT prompt generator</a> and <a href="/claude-prompt-generator" class="text-[#1a1a1a] underline decoration-[#f0b429] underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#f0b429]">Claude prompt generator</a> to build better prompts from scratch.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="border border-[#c8c0a8] rounded-xl p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#1a1a1a] mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div>
          <p class="font-semibold text-[#1a1a1a] text-sm">How does this prompt quality checker work?</p>
          <p class="text-[#6b6559] text-xs mt-1">It analyses your prompt across five dimensions — clarity, specificity, context, format, and constraints — and scores each one based on what's present and what's missing. The improved version applies fixes automatically.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-semibold text-[#1a1a1a] text-sm">Does it work for ChatGPT, Claude, and other models?</p>
          <p class="text-[#6b6559] text-xs mt-1">Yes — the five dimensions apply to any large language model. The principles that make a prompt work (clear task, specific requirements, format instructions) are consistent across ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, and others.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-semibold text-[#1a1a1a] text-sm">What score should I aim for?</p>
          <p class="text-[#6b6559] text-xs mt-1">7 or above consistently produces noticeably better output. Scores of 4–6 usually mean one or two specific dimensions are dragging down otherwise solid prompts — the fixes section will point to exactly what to change.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-semibold text-[#1a1a1a] text-sm">Can I rate my prompt more than once?</p>
          <p class="text-[#6b6559] text-xs mt-1">Yes — paste in your improved version and roast it again. The score should climb as you apply the fixes. It's a useful iteration loop for prompts you use repeatedly.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <a href="#root" class="block w-full py-4 bg-[#f0b429] border-2 border-[#1c1c1c] rounded-xl text-center font-bold text-[#1a1a1a] text-lg hover:brightness-95 transition-all">
      Roast My Prompt
    </a>
  </div>

    <PricingSection client:load priceIds={{
      starterMonthly: import.meta.env.STRIPE_PRICE_STARTER_MONTHLY,
      starterYearly: import.meta.env.STRIPE_PRICE_STARTER_YEARLY,
      proMonthly: import.meta.env.STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_MONTHLY,
      proYearly: import.meta.env.STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_YEARLY,
      unlimitedMonthly: import.meta.env.STRIPE_PRICE_UNLIMITED_MONTHLY,
      unlimitedYearly: import.meta.env.STRIPE_PRICE_UNLIMITED_YEARLY,
    }} />
</Layout>
